'' ===========================================================================
''
''   File.......  ch12-mouse-pointer.spin2
''   Purpose....  Mouse position and buttons reported live, with the
''                window as the pointing device
''   Manual.....  P2 Debug Window Manual
''   Version....  v1.1.3 (2026-08-18)
''   Appears in.  Chapter 12: Bidirectional Control - Keyboard and Mouse
''                -- PC_MOUSE - reading the mouse
''   Authors....  Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''   E-mail.....  stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started....  Jun 2026
''   Updated....  Jul 2026
''
''   This file is an EXAMPLE from the manual above. Everything below
''   this header is byte-identical to the listing printed there --
''   what you read in the manual is what builds here.
''
'' ===========================================================================

CON _clkfreq = 200_000_000

PUB main() | mouse[7]
  debug(`TERM Pointer SIZE 40 8 TITLE 'Mouse State')
  repeat
    debug(`Pointer `PC_MOUSE(@mouse))
    debug(`Pointer 0)                                 ' clear + home
    if mouse[0] < 0
      debug(`Pointer 'Pointer outside window' 13)
    else
      debug(`Pointer 'X: `(mouse[0])  Y: `(mouse[1])' 13)
      debug(`Pointer 'Wheel: `(mouse[2])' 13)
      debug(`Pointer 'Buttons  L:`(mouse[3])')
      debug(`Pointer '  M:`(mouse[4])  R:`(mouse[5])' 13)
      debug(`Pointer 'Pixel: `$(mouse[6])')
    if mouse[3]                                        ' left button down?
      debug(`Pointer 13 'LEFT DOWN')
    waitms(30)

